eu countries have reached a deal on  making emergency gas cuts this winter  europe is facing an energy crisis as the  russian-owned firm gazprom reduces  supplies from the nordstream 1 pipeline  from wednesday supplies will be just 20  of capacity half  of what they were in june  european energy ministers have held an  emergency meeting in brussels to discuss  their response russia says the  disruption is due to maintenance issues  and sanctions but the eu disputes that  we know that there is no technical  reason to do so this is a politically  motivated step and we have to be ready  for that and exactly for that reason  preemptive reduction of our gas demand  is a a wise  strategy  live now to brussels al jazeera's  abdullah al-shami joins us from there so  abdullah um what exactly of eu ministers  agreed  well the the the agreement that came  just um in an hour ago it was uh based  on the fact that uh all these state  members will go through a voluntary  reduction of their gas consumption  starting from the 1st of august all the  way till the 1st of march  2023  this voluntary reduction would be turned  into a mandatory one if the eu as cited  in the statement that came out if the eu  sees a security alert or security threat  to its uh gas supplies it will indeed  turn this into uh this uh mandatory uh  way of enforcing these cuts the eu aims  to store about 45 billion cubes cubic  meters of gas for this next winter and  at the same time the eu has also given  exemptions to member states who are not  part of the european gas network and  indeed at that point they will not have  to enforce the  mandatory gas costs if it has to come to  it so the eu has been able to kind of  come to midway between the countries  that saw it as you know  not really possible to enforce this kind  of mandatory cuts at the same time being  able to secure what it says it needs for  the next winter abdullah how was this  deal reached were eu states unified in  their response  well uh at the beginning of this meeting  this morning there was no uh that sense  of unity we we've seen countries like  portugal and poland as well as countries  from central europe uh as hungary that  in fact even threatened to go on its own  and have its own separate agreements  with russia because the eu handles  through the commission all the  agreements in terms of the power  supplies and the energy supplies in  general so the eu was able to come this  agreement after kind of conceding the  the part where it comes to mandatory  cuts uh it it said that these uh  these cuts will not be imposed uh for  the countries that has their own uh  special needs as cited in the statement  and at the same time it also gave the  option that if five countries or five  members of the eu ask for this cuts to  be imposed that will also happen so it  was that midpoint that the eu  you know has been able to reach just  a few uh minutes before the start of the  press conference in which uh this  statement will be announced officially  and thus it probably will be able to  save that is needed for the next winter  but still the eu commissioner for energy  says that they are ready for anything  that comes out of russia if that  disruption happens they are ready and  they are already waiting uh for supplies  that will come very soon from outside of  the european continent from countries  like egypt and israel al jazeera's  abdullah al-shami reporting live there  from brussels abdullah many thanks  indeed well that eu meeting came just  hours after ukraine's president vladimir  zelinski again accused russia of  inflicting what he called terror on  europe by restricting gas supplies  today we saw a new gas threat to europe  despite the nordstrom turbine concession  russia is not planning to resume gas  supply to european countries as it is  obliged to do all this is done by russia  on purpose there is an open gas war that  russia is waging against united europe  they do not care what will happen to the  people how they will suffer from hunger  due to the blocking of ports or from  winter cold and poverty or from  occupation these are just different  forms of terror
 

